Us for different reordering strategies, focusing on both sequential and parallel execution.\nL17: We address multiple aspects, including appropriate measurement methodology, comparison across different kinds of reordering strategies, consistency across machines, and impact of load imbalance.\nL18: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC); Performance (cs.PF)\nL19: Cite as:  | 【13†arXiv:2506.10356】 [cs.DC]\nL20:    | (or 【14†arXiv:2506.10356v2】 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL21:    | 【15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2506.10356†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Omid Asudeh [【16†view email】]\nL25: 【5†[v1]】 Thu, 12 Jun 2025 05:29:39 UTC (4,404 KB)\nL26: [v2] Sun, 21 Sep 2025 18:11:26 UTC (907 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Is Sparse Matrix Reordering Effective for Sparse Matrix-Vector Multiplication?, by Omid Asudeh and 4 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * 【11†View PDF】\nL35:   * 【12†HTML (experimental)】\nL36:   * 【17†TeX Source】\nL37: \nL38: 【18†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL39: \nL40: ### Additional Features\nL41: \nL42:   * 【19†Audio Summary】\nL43: ### Current browse context:\nL44: \nL45: cs.DC\nL46: \nL47: 【20†< prev】   |   【21†next >】\nL48: \nL49: 【22†new】 | 【23†recent】 | 【24†2025-06】\nL50: \nL51: Change to browse by:\nL52: \nL53: 【25†cs】\nL54: 【26†cs.PF】\nL55: \nL56: ### References & Citations\nL57: \nL58:   * 【27†SciX†scixplorer.org】\nL59:   * 【28†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL60:   * 【29†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL61: \nL62: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL63: \nL64: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL65: \nL66: [Button: ×]\nL67: \nL68: loading...\nL69: \nL70: Data provided by:\nL71: \nL72: ### Bookmark\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL75: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Bibliographic Explorer (【30†Wh